question (producer decision, blocks closure): AC3 reads "A fresh run of `npm run validate-experience -- eval-output/balance-report.json` produces output in `experience-out/` and leaves `git status --porcelain` clean", but `eval-output/balance-report.json` does not exist in the repo (eval-output/ is git-ignored and holds no file at that exact path), so the criterion cannot be satisfied literally from a clean checkout. The auditor has now demonstrated the underlying behaviour with a real bot-batch report (see the AC3 re-verification comment). Which do you want?

(a) Accept the auditor's evidence as satisfying AC3 and re-audit/close the item as-is;
(b) Reword AC3 to name an input that exists or is generated (e.g. `eval-output/rerun-baseline-2026-11-07/balance-report.json`, or "any `kind: balance` report") — requires an implement session to amend the work item;
(c) Leave the item open at `open`/`plan_complete`.

No further action has been taken: this audit does not edit work items beyond its own report.
